### PASS A: VANILLA ###

In the heart of a stormy coast stood Lighthouse Keepers' Cottage, its light piercing through the fog. Elias had lived here for over two decades but had never set foot on the sea. His days were spent tending to the lamp, his nights filled with the rhythmic crashing against the cliffs below. One evening, as he climbed the tower, a sudden calm settled. The wind whispered secrets of distant waves. At last, driven by an inexplicable urge, Elias descended into the shore. There, under the moonlight, he saw the vast expanse of water—blue and endless, alive with stories untold. He realized that while the sea was beyond him, it was always within reach, just like hope.

